            <ArticleTitle>Clinical analgesic assay of oral zomepirac and intramuscular morphine.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>261-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Zomepirac appears to be an unexpectedly effective oral, non-opioid analgesic. The relative potency of oral zomepirac is roughly 1/5 to 1/8 that of intramuscular morphine. Visual analogues of pain relief offer a reliable alternative to verbal categorical scales, and may provide some advantages in assays of peak drug effect, and in relatively small patient populations.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
